Bind the IPv6 ICE components like the IPv4 ones.

pjsua builds the bound address of an IPv6 ICE STUN or TURN transport from the
string "0" (IN6_ADDR_ANY) and ignores the account's bound address, which only
the IPv4 components use. pj_sockaddr_init(AF_INET6, "0") is not an IPv6
literal, so pjlib falls back to getaddrinfo, which on macOS returns the
IPv4-mapped ::ffff:0.0.0.0. Binding that to an IPv6 socket with IPV6_V6ONLY set
(as pjlib does) fails with EADDRNOTAVAIL ("Failed creating STUN transport #1
... Can't assign requested address"): an IPv6 call with ICE then has IPv4
candidates only and fails on an IPv6 answer.

- The IPv6 components bind to the account's bound address when that is an IPv6
  address, otherwise to "::" (the IPv6 any address, parsed by inet_pton).
- A STUN component bound to a loopback address on purpose keeps its host
  candidate (loop_addr); pjnath leaves loopback candidates out by default, so a
  loopback bound address would leave the component without any candidate.

MacroSIP: applied by scripts/build-pjsip.sh (ADR 0014).

--- a/pjsip/src/pjsua-lib/pjsua_media.c
